# NOTES: Law 08/2022/QH15 on Insurance Business, three vintages, in L4

Row `legalese-2026-10-vn-29`, run `VN-29-20261010`, encoder `enc-vn-29` (one agent, one session, no sub-agents, from `BRIEF.md`).
Status: **draft**, version **0.1.0**. Nothing here is legal advice. No Vietnamese-qualified lawyer has read it; gate HG1 has not been sought.
The authoritative texts are the three gazette files (`law08-2022-qh15.txt`, `law08-2022-qh15-577-578.txt`, `law139-2025-qh15.txt`). No consolidated text was used. **The applied text of V2 and V3 is the encoder's own application of the amending Law to V1**: where a module has a V2 or V3 arm, the arm cites the source lines of the amending Law that supply it (`src:law139-2025-qh15:N`) and the V1 arm cites the lines of the Law as made.

## 0. Build and run

- `l4`: the build that `~/.local/bin/l4` pointed to on 2026-10-10 (a symlink to `~/.cabal/bin/l4`, cabal store `jl4-0.1-a76e8866`), sha256 `db2c66fda1d2e30a5182fd3d60add141bd0e40cf09b14f6eb68772ce947797d7`; a copy of that binary was put first on `PATH` for the run so that it could not change under it, and the lead re-ran `./check.sh` and `vnsrc.py check` with it after the run and got the same totals. `JL4_LIBRARY_PATH` unset. `l4` has no `--version` flag.
- The modules are generated. Each is written as `templates/NAME.l4.in`, where a line `@@q N M` is expanded by `tools/expand.py` into the `-- src:N | ...` lines (through `tools/vnsrc.py`'s own quote routine) and a line `@@fx` into a complete test fixture (every field of the record, `FALSE`, `0`, `YMD 2000 1 1`, `NOTHING` or `EMPTY` unless given). So no Vietnamese in a module was typed by hand, and a fixture cannot omit a field silently. To rebuild: `python3 -I tools/expand.py`, then `./check.sh`.
- `NOTES.md` is generated by `python3 -I tools/gen_notes.py` from `templates/NOTES.md.in`, `templates/coverage.tsv` and `tools/notes_data.py`; `GLOSSARY.md` by `python3 -I tools/gen_glossary.py`; `encoding.json` and `SOURCE-LICENSE.md` by the same script as NOTES.md. The numbers in this file (the `check.sh` table, the roadmap lines, the `vnsrc` line) are the tools' output at the time it was generated, not typed.
- Run: `./check.sh` (one `l4` process at a time). Whole run: about 45 seconds on this machine for all modules; the slowest single module (`law08-tests-findings.l4`) takes about 3 seconds. No module needed splitting for time.
- Run record, from the CLI's own result event: wall clock 4,956 s (82.6 minutes) from 2026-10-10 17:38 +08; 215 turns; total cost USD 29.62, of which the CLI reported `claude-sonnet-5-5` USD 19.38 and `claude-fable-5-1` USD 10.23; the session's init event named only `claude-sonnet-5-5`, and the tool log has 214 tool calls (Read 22, Bash 132, Grep 9, Write 45, Edit 5, Glob 1) and no sub-agent call. The `claude-fable-5-1` share is reported by the CLI and is not explained here.
- Second run record, the fork register: the same session was resumed on 2026-10-10 (about 21:45 +08, 16 turns, 423 s) to write `registers/fork-register.json` and `tools/make_fork_register.py`. Its result event reports a cumulative total of USD 34.86, of which `claude-sonnet-5-5` USD 24.63 and `claude-fable-5-1` USD 10.23; the Fable figure is identical to the first run's, so the resumed turns added about USD 5.25, all on `claude-sonnet-5-5`. The cumulative figure is the CLI's; the split between the two runs is the lead's subtraction.
- The import graph is a shallow tree, not a long chain: `law08-vintage` (imports daydate) and `law08-nouns` (prelude, daydate) are at the root; every rule module imports both; `law08-ch2-general` also imports `law08-ch3-scope` (for Điều 15(2) and 63(3)), and `law08-ch2-life-health` and `law08-ch2-property` import `law08-ch2-general`; `law08-ch3-finance`, `law08-ch3-solvency` and `law08-ch5-ch6-micro-state` also import `law08-ch7-commencement` (for the deferred commencements of Điều 156(2)); each tests module imports the module it tests. No rule module imports a tests module. `law08-tests-findings` imports every rule module except `law08-ch3-scope` (which it reaches through `law08-ch2-general`) and is the slowest to check.
